---
title: "Consent lifecycle (the corrected behaviour)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> NoConsent: invitation redeemed,<br/>Borrower Profile created

  NoConsent --> ConsentHeld: accept terms + privacy<br/>in the wizard review step
  note right of ConsentHeld
    consent_terms = 1, consent_privacy = 1
    consent_at = now  first real acceptance
  end note

  ConsentHeld --> ConsentHeld: ordinary profile edit<br/>(income, employer, locale, literacy)
  note right of ConsentHeld
    THE FIX: an unrelated save leaves consent_at alone.
    Before it, every save of the document restamped
    consent_at, so "last save" masqueraded as consent.
    Regression tests: test_consent.py, and the browser
    check tests/e2e/consent_regression_e2e.cjs
  end note

  ConsentHeld --> ConsentHeld: resending the same checkboxes,<br/>unchanged
  note right of ConsentHeld: not a new consent event

  ConsentHeld --> Revoked: borrower withdraws an agreement
  Revoked --> ConsentHeld: re-accept<br/>consent_at moves, deliberately

  ConsentHeld --> ConsentHeld: new notice version published<br/>(e.g. voice-consent/1)
  note right of ConsentHeld
    A new version is a separate acceptance. The voice
    notice stores its own consent_version and consent_at
    on VoiceSession, so agreeing to voice is visible and
    dated independently of the account-level consent.
  end note

  ConsentHeld --> [*]: profile closed
